1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:05,114
When a website breaks, real people feel it.

2
00:00:05,364 --> 00:00:06,695
Shoppers can't pay.

3
00:00:06,945 --> 00:00:11,615
And someone on the team has to fix it fast, often in the middle of the night.

4
00:00:12,565 --> 00:00:13,668
That's hard.

5
00:00:13,918 --> 00:00:16,780
The clues are spread across many different tools.

6
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:21,838
And some AI helpers guess, or even make changes that nobody agreed to.

7
00:00:22,788 --> 00:00:24,934
Meet AI Incident Commander.

8
00:00:25,184 --> 00:00:27,232
It puts everything in one place.

9
00:00:27,482 --> 00:00:32,156
This screen shows what is broken right now, and it updates on its own.

10
00:00:33,106 --> 00:00:35,515
Every problem shows up in one list.

11
00:00:35,765 --> 00:00:40,540
If the same problem is reported fifty times, you only see it once.

12
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:43,215
The most serious ones stay at the top.

13
00:00:44,165 --> 00:00:45,699
Bob is on call today.

14
00:00:45,949 --> 00:00:49,421
Bob opens the checkout problem and clicks Acknowledge.

15
00:00:49,671 --> 00:00:52,102
Now the whole team knows who is on it.

16
00:00:53,052 --> 00:00:55,449
The AI has already done the homework.

17
00:00:55,699 --> 00:01:00,723
It read the error messages, the recent updates, and the team's own guides.

18
00:01:00,973 --> 00:01:04,118
It thinks a new update probably caused the problem.

19
00:01:04,368 --> 00:01:06,987
And it shows the proof for every point.

20
00:01:07,937 --> 00:01:10,798
Passwords and secret keys are hidden automatically.

21
00:01:11,048 --> 00:01:13,177
Nobody sees them by accident.

22
00:01:13,427 --> 00:01:14,940
Not even the AI.

23
00:01:15,890 --> 00:01:19,599
The AI suggests going back to the last version that worked.

24
00:01:19,849 --> 00:01:22,168
But the AI can't do that by itself.

25
00:01:22,418 --> 00:01:24,332
Bob sends it as a request.

26
00:01:24,582 --> 00:01:28,338
In this demo, fixes run on a safe practice system.

27
00:01:29,288 --> 00:01:31,674
Now a second person must say yes.

28
00:01:31,924 --> 00:01:34,355
The person who asked can't approve it.

29
00:01:34,605 --> 00:01:39,279
So Carol checks the details, writes a short reason, and approves.

30
00:01:41,529 --> 00:01:45,029
Right before the fix runs, everything is checked again.

31
00:01:45,279 --> 00:01:48,226
Then it runs once, and only once.

32
00:01:48,476 --> 00:01:53,373
And every step is saved, so anyone can see who did what, and why.

33
00:01:54,323 --> 00:01:56,411
It works on your phone, too.

34
00:01:56,661 --> 00:01:58,554
So help is always close by.

35
00:01:59,504 --> 00:02:01,715
Engineers find answers faster.

36
00:02:01,965 --> 00:02:04,578
Managers get a safe way to say yes.

37
00:02:04,828 --> 00:02:09,413
And companies get shorter outages, with a clear record of what happened.

38
00:02:10,663 --> 00:02:12,945
This is AI Incident Commander.

39
00:02:13,195 --> 00:02:15,021
The AI does the homework.

40
00:02:15,271 --> 00:02:16,950
People make the decisions.

